		"factions": [
			{
				"name": "Bolschev",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Overloading: Once per Game Round, during the Maneuvering or Gunnery Phase, a Bolschev Pilt may Stress their Reactor even if it is already at Maximum Stress. If they do, Frame takes single point of Damage to the Body; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.25\n Propulsion Types: Tracked, Multi-Limbed, Bipedal"
				]
			},
			{
				"name": "Ghosts of Tiamat",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Deus Ex Machina: Pilots cannot be Aces and always deploy Trained Pilots. Pilots do not take Damage during the Cool-Down Phase when their Frame is Critically Damaged in the Body but do suffer Inguries from additional Damage to their Frame. When Injured, do not suffer any penalties to Tests and recover from Injuries as usual between Missions. During Cool-Down Phase, they receive +1 to their Technical Tests; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.27\n Propulsion Types: Any"
				]
			},
			{
				"name": "Hinode",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Masters and Apprentices: Must include 1 Rookie Pilot per Trained or Veteran Pilot which is assigned as the Master. Both the Master and Rookie Pilots must be in the same size Frame. Whenever the Rookie Pilot performs a Gunnery, Evasion, or Maneuver Test while their Master has Lock to them, they receive +1 to the results of their Test Roll; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.28\n Propulsion Types: Multi-Limbed, Bipedal, Jet"
				]
			},
			{
				"name": "North-Star",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Meat for the Grinder: May never have more Veteran or Trained Pilots than Rooke Pilots. When a Veteran or Trained Pilot performs an Evasion Test and a Rookie Pilot has Lock wit the active Frame, they receive +1 to the Evasion Roll and the Rookie Pilot's Frame automatically takes a point of Damage to a random Location; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.29\n Propulsion Types: Any"
				]
			},
			{
				"name": "Ronin",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Smokin' Aces: Any number of Pilots may be Aces; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.29\n Propulsion Types: Any"
				]
			},
			{
				"name": "The Burg",
				"additionalRules": [
					"Humanity 2.0: Pilots do not take Damage during the Cool-Down Phase when their Frame is Critically Damaged in the Body but do suffer Inguries from additional Damage to their Frame during an Engagement; Gamma Wolves Rulebook pg.26\n Propulsion Types: Any"
				]
			}
		],
